<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tukulti-Ninurta I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tukulti-Ninurta I was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> in the thirteenth century BCE, one of the most powerful rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-assyrian-empire">Middle Assyrian</a> period. The Assyrian Empire profile highlights his conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> around 1225 BCE and his personal capture of the Kassite king. He also founded a new royal city, Kar-Tukulti-Ninurta, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tukulti-ninurta-i.jpg" alt="Tukulti-Ninurta I" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detail._Assyrian_king_Tukulti-Ninurta_I_stands_and_kneels,_13th_century_BCE._From_Assur,_Iraq._Pergamon_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
